{
  "dn17:0.1": "Long Discourses 17 ",
  "dn17:0.2": "King Mahāsudassana ",
  "dn17:1.1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "dn17:1.1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying between a pair of sal trees in the sal forest of the Mallas at Upavattana near Kusinārā at the time of his full extinguishment. ",
  "dn17:1.2.1": "Then Venerable Ānanda went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "dn17:1.2.2": "“Sir, please don’t be fully extinguished in this little hamlet, this jungle hamlet, this branch hamlet. ",
  "dn17:1.2.3": "There are other great cities such as ",
  "dn17:1.2.4": "Campā, Rājagaha, Sāvatthī, Sāketa, Kosambī, and Varanasi. ",
  "dn17:1.2.5": "Let the Buddha be fully extinguished there. ",
  "dn17:1.2.6": "There are many well-to-do aristocrats, brahmins, and householders there who are devoted to the Buddha. They will perform the rites of venerating the Realized One’s corpse.” ",
  "dn17:1.3.1": "“Don’t say that, Ānanda! Don’t say that ",
  "dn17:1.3.2": "this is a little hamlet, a jungle hamlet, a branch hamlet. ",
  "dn17:1.3.3.0": "1. The Capital City of Kusāvatī ",
  "dn17:1.3.4": "Once upon a time, there was a king named Mahāsudassana whose dominion extended to all four sides, and who achieved stability in the country. ",
  "dn17:1.3.5": "His capital was this Kusinārā, which at the time was named Kusāvatī. ",
  "dn17:1.3.6": "It stretched for twelve leagues from east to west, and seven leagues from north to south. ",
